id: pm-graph-4hs4
title: Classify missing optional Neo4j configuration as an expected CLI error
description: "Use pm-graph's package-safe expected-error contract for query and neighbors when optional Neo4j environment configuration is absent, so pm-cli returns actionable usage guidance without reporting a release-blocking operational fault to Sentry."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: neo4j,release-gate,sentry,telemetry
created_at: "2026-07-15T07:03:49.420Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-15T11:42:24.982Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-15T11:42:24.721Z"
author: codex-root
resolution: Classified absent optional Neo4j environment configuration as a package-safe PmCliError with USAGE exit code 2.
expected_result: "Query, neighbors, and sync explain missing Neo4j variables through one package-safe usage error without producing an operational Sentry event."
actual_result: "createDriver now owns the configuration guard for every Neo4j-backed command; real CLI acceptance covers sync, query, and neighbors at exit code 2."
affected_version: 2026.7.14-1
component: extension error contract
regression: true
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-15T07:03:49.420Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check: all-status searches for Neo4j missing configuration, expected error, exit code, telemetry, and Sentry found no existing item for this classification defect. Related closed pm-graph-1fr9 covers positional command contracts; pm-cli owner item pm-7n5a tracks the ecosystem symptom."
  "2026-07-15T07:09:40.342Z",codex-root,"Evidence: package CommandError now uses the public structural PmCliError discriminant; query and neighbors return USAGE exit 2 when optional Neo4j configuration is missing. Real pm CLI acceptance assertions passed within 67/67 tests. Typecheck/build, zero-vulnerability production audit, package dry-run, and changelog check also passed."
  "2026-07-15T11:42:24.484Z",codex,"Review correction evidence: accepted Gemini's high-priority PR #25 finding. createDriver now centralizes missing Neo4j configuration as PmCliError/USAGE, redundant query and neighbors guards are removed, and sync receives real CLI acceptance coverage. npm run release:check passed typecheck/build, 68/68 tests, zero-vulnerability production audit, and package dry-run; changelog regeneration follows the final tracker mutation."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
